Accept the RTP/AVP/UDP transport specification

ffmpeg, VLC and mpv send an explicit lower-transport (RTP/AVP/UDP) on
UDP SETUP. Since 2026.x the parser matches transport-specs exactly and
no longer defaults an unrecognized spec to UDP, so RTP/AVP/UDP leaves
the streaming mode UNKNOWN and the request is answered 461. RFC 2326
12.39 makes the lower-transport optional and UDP its default, so
RTP/AVP/UDP is equivalent to RTP/AVP. Recognize it. (Upstream-worthy.)

--- a/liveMedia/RTSPServer.cpp	2026-07-23 09:42:04.000000000 -0700
+++ b/liveMedia/RTSPServer.cpp	2026-07-29 16:22:24.518451505 -0700
@@ -1360,7 +1360,8 @@
       if (streamingMode != UNKNOWN) break; // more than one 'streaming mode' is not allowed
 
       streamingMode = RTP_TCP;
-    } else if (strcmp(field, "RTP/AVP") == 0 || strcmp(field, "RTP/AVP/SAVP") == 0) {
+    } else if (strcmp(field, "RTP/AVP") == 0 || strcmp(field, "RTP/AVP/UDP") == 0 ||
+	       strcmp(field, "RTP/AVP/SAVP") == 0) {
       if (streamingMode != UNKNOWN) break; // more than one 'streaming mode' is not allowed
 
       streamingMode = RTP_UDP;
